"""
Project: Superconducting state

Description:

CDMFT-ED calculation for the superconducting state of a 2x2 plaquette cluster using the pyqcm package.

Authors:
- Vitor Assunção Moreira Lima (vitor.aml@hotmail.com)
-

Created: 2026-04-08
Last Modified: 2026-04-08
Version: 1.0.0

License: MIT 

Dependencies:
- Python > 3.10.x
- pyqcm >= 2.10.4
- pandas >= ?

Usage example:
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 python3 cdmft.py > out_cdmft

Structure:
This folder contains:
i) cdmft.py: Input values, the main part of the CMDFT run and output generating functions;
ii) model.py: Defines the cluster geometry and the lattice model parameters;
iii) cluster.py: Defines the bath parametrization and creates the cluster model;

The cdmft.py script uses model.py, that requires cluster.py. For the superconducting state we would use a general C2 bath symmetry. A converged calculation is present in 'solved' folder with some basic outputs. For a full output display check the 'output_full' folder inside 'solved'.

For more information please go to the official documentation website https://qcm-wed.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html!
"""
